Skia m153 (rust-skia/skia m153-0.101.2): build Graphite's Dawn backend for wasm against Dawn's emdawnwebgpu
Emscripten port instead of native Dawn. Applied by .github/workflows/build.yml; build with
-DSKIA_USING_EMDAWNWEBGPU and emcc --use-port=<emdawnwebgpu_pkg>/emdawnwebgpu.port.py.

- third_party/dawn/BUILD.gn: on wasm, no native Dawn CMake build or library (the port supplies webgpu.h and wgpu*).
- src/gpu/graphite/dawn: the `__EMSCRIPTEN__` branches target emscripten's removed -sUSE_WEBGPU headers;
  emdawnwebgpu ships the current Dawn API, so those sites take the native branch under SKIA_USING_EMDAWNWEBGPU.
  Same sites as SkiaSharp's mono/skia fork (2ef241b9).
- gn/toolchain/BUILD.gn: emsdk 6 on Windows ships emcc.exe launchers, not emcc.bat.

